<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN SPADEL SWINGS TO H1 1996 PROFIT.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN SPADEL SWINGS TO H1 1996 PROFIT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit		   123  vs     7 loss</p>
<p>    Cons turnover		    4,420  vs 4,196</p>
<p>    Cash flow			    735  vs   513</p>
<p>    Taxes				  128  vs    48</p>
<p>NOTE - Spadel is a Belgian mineral waters group.</p>
<p>In a statement Spadel said it hoped that lower raw material</p>
<p>prices in the second half would allow it to compensate for a</p>
<p>drop in summer sales and return a full year profit &quot;at least</p>
<p>equal to that of 1995&quot;.</p>
<p>Spadel said poor weather in July and August had left sales</p>
<p>at the end of August nine percent down on 1995 levels. &quot;This</p>
<p>decrease cannot be recovered this year,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Spadel said results in 1996 and subsequent years should also</p>
<p>be helped by the abolition of certain direct taxes on mineral</p>
<p>water and lower sales taxes.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax</p>
<p>+32 2 230 7710</p>
